    "updated_at": "2023-07-13T08:34:13Z",
    "body": "Thank you to Olli for not letting this be a solo meeting today! Here are the notes from this meeting (the next one is at https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/9515):\r\n\r\n### Agenda  \r\nAttendees: Panos Astithas, Olli Pettay\r\n\r\n1. Review past action items\r\n    1. Olli will take a look at the latest changes in [Update the :dir / directionality to include shadow dom](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/9166). Mason and Joey will take another review pass.\r\n        1. Several comments and feedback from Mason, Anne, Elika and Olli.\r\n        1. Waiting for the PR to be updated now\r\n    1. Mason will find someone from Chrome to review [Reference even more baseline concepts in CSS Inline Layout](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/5826).\r\n        1. Folks were tagged, but no review yet.\r\n    1. Mason will add the \"addition/proposal\" label to the non-blocking [issues for Popover](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues?q=is%3Aissue+is%3Aopen+label%3A%22topic%3A+popover%22).\r\n        1. Not done yet.\r\n    1. Panos to ask the CSS and a11y folks if they want to meet jointly at TPAC and file an issue with a proposed agenda.\r\n        1. CSSWG agreed to have a joint session and we are discussing the details. Filed an [issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/issues/284) for agenda discussions.\r\n1. Carryovers from last time\r\n    1. None\r\n1. New topics\r\n    1. None\r\n\r\n### Action Items\r\n\r\n1. @bkardell will address review feedback on [Update the :dir / directionality to include shadow dom](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/9166).\r\n1. @yiyix will review [Reference even more baseline concepts in CSS Inline Layout](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/5826).\r\n1. @mfreed7 will add the \"addition/proposal\" label to the non-blocking [issues for Popover](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues?q=is%3Aissue+is%3Aopen+label%3A%22topic%3A+popover%22).",
